---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · bruhs"
  description="The bruhs.ai website collects nothing about you. What the bruhs app sends online, and where downloads come from."
  path="/privacy"
  current="privacy"
  fonts={[]}
>
  <main id="main" class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>This page covers the bruhs.ai website and the downloads it links to. The bruhs app keeps your data on your device; the <a href="/#privacy">privacy section</a> of the home page lists what goes online.</p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>The site has no forms, no cookies, no analytics and no tracking pixels. It is hosted on Vercel, which keeps standard request logs (such as IP address and time) for operating the service.</p>

      <h2>Downloads and updates</h2>
      <p>Downloads and source code come from GitHub, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its own privacy statement</a>. The app checks GitHub for a newer release, and npm or Homebrew for newer Claude Code and Codex CLIs, unless you turn off <strong>Check for updates</strong> in Settings → Updates. Those checks send no account or usage data.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:privacy@bruhs.ai">privacy@bruhs.ai</a>, or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/bryantleft/bruhs-ai">GitHub</a>.</p>

      <p class="subtle">Last updated November 8, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
